  "notes": "COMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {利上|りあ}げを{決定|けってい}する (decide to raise rates)\n- {追加|ついか}{利上|りあ}げ (additional rate hike)\n- {利上|りあ}げ{幅|はば} (size of the rate increase)\n- {利上|りあ}げ{観測|かんそく} (rate hike expectations)\n\nUSAGE:\nThe opposite is {利下|りさ}げ (interest rate cut). In Japanese economic news, {利上|りあ}げ most commonly refers to actions by the {日本銀行|にほんぎんこう} (Bank of Japan) or foreign central banks like the FRB (Federal Reserve). The word is an abbreviation of {金利引|きんりひ}き{上|あ}げ.",
